 { Black to move. Can he draw ? } 89... Be4 $1 { Yes. } ( { Dominguez - Bruzon, Havana 2005 continued } 89... Kb6 $2 90. f5 { Now one of the diagonals is 4 squares long and Black is lost in any case, but anyway, the Bishop cannot stop the pawn anymore. } Kxa7 $6 91. Ne7 $1 { 1-0 } ) 
90. Ne7 Kb7 $11 { The Black King captures the a7 pawn and the Bishop is able to stop the f-pawn, because both control diagonals are more than 4 squares long. } 
